  "articleBody": "When a Texas storm rolls through, it can leave behind more than just downed branches; your roof could be hiding damage you can't see from the ground. A professional roof damage assessment isn't just about patching up a leak; it's about understanding the full extent of the issue, what caused it, and what it takes to restore your roof's integrity. It can feel overwhelming, but getting a clear, expert assessment is your first step to peace of mind.\n\nFirst, a thorough assessment goes beyond the obvious. We'll look for signs of hail damage, wind uplift, or debris impact across all accessible roof planes, not just the visibly affected ones. We’ll also check critical areas like gutters, flashing, and penetrations, plus interior spaces for any water intrusion, even subtle ones.\n\nThe goal is to identify what was damaged and its likely cause – was it hail, wind, or just normal aging? We focus on separating storm-related damage from pre-existing conditions or general wear and tear, which is super important when dealing with insurance claims.\n\nDocumentation is key here. We'll take dated, high-resolution photographs, both wide context views and close-ups, to clearly show the damage. This documentation is vital for your records and for any potential insurance claims you might need to file.\n\nFinally, a good assessment provides clear repair or replacement recommendations based on our findings. We'll give you an honest appraisal of what's repairable versus what might need a broader replacement, along with an estimate for the scope of work.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process\n\nWhen we conduct a damage assessment, we'll confirm property details, review any reported loss dates or weather events, and perform a safe perimeter inspection before getting on the roof. We map out accessible roof planes, check all related components, look for interior water intrusion, and then provide a detailed written assessment. Our priority is a clear, accurate picture of your roof's health.\n\nWhat to Do Next\n\nIf your roof has been through a storm and you need an expert assessment, don't wait. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a reliable and honest evaluation. We're here to help guide you through the process.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}